.TH GIT-DIFF-STAGED-VS 1 "2026-10-01" "Git Helpers" "git-helpers Manual"
.SH NAME
git-diff-staged-vs \- compare staged changes against a commit or ref
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git diff-staged-vs
[IrefnameR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgit-diff-staged-vs\fR compares the current staged patch against a commit,
merge state, or other ref. By default it uses \fBREBASE_HEAD\fR when no ref name
is supplied, making it handy during rebases and review workflows.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B git diff-staged-vs HEAD~1
Compare the staged diff to the previous commit.
.TP
.B git diff-staged-vs REBASE_HEAD
Compare the staged changes against the in-progress rebase target.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git-difftool (1)
